verdict.evidence:
S8 matches the spec and works. I found only three minor problems: one error message that no longer names its field, and two small test gaps.

I checked branch p2-s8 at e2ac479 in fresh scratch copies taken with git archive (verify-S8-1/2/3, under <scratch>/p2-scratch/). I read spec §0 (R1-R11), §2, §3.2-3.5, §5.2, §6.1, §8, §10.2 (S8, plus S5 and S7 for file overlap), §12 and the appendix.

Scope:
- The diff touches only S8's files: ledger/genesis.go, ledger/genesis_test.go, cmd/server/config.go, config_test.go and main.go (doc comment only), and cmd/demo/main.go and main_test.go. Nothing of S5's or S7's is touched.
- ValidateGenesis applies all eight rules of §2.2:
  - networkName and account names canonical, with no duplicates;
  - keys canonical and 1952 bytes, with no duplicates;
  - amounts parse and stay within maxAccountBalance, zero allowed;
  - every delegate is "" or an account;
  - no account is its own bank, and every bank is seated (R2, R4);
  - static mode: validators are accounts, listed once, power at least 1; dynamic mode: a threshold above 0; never both modes, never neither;
  - Acceptable is checked against the seated count;
  - at least one name is seated.
- It returns the §2.3 state (accounts in name order, height 0, sequence 0), the genesis hash, and the id name/hex.
- The node config has the §8.2 shape, and unknown keys are refused. The topology is built from the genesis addresses. The demo matches §8.3.
- Nothing from a later slice is half-built. The deviations are justified, apart from deviation 4 (reported above).

Adversarial tests (scratch copy verify-S8-2):
- Refused, with clear errors:
  - trailing data after the JSON;
  - a null or missing parameters object;
  - wrongly typed or fractional integer parameters, such as 0.5 or 8.64e4;
  - names ending in \n;
  - keys with an embedded \n;
  - a "-" delegate or bank;
  - a validator listed twice through a key in another case;
  - a threshold of 0.5 with stakes below 1 (refused as "seats no name");
  - both modes at once.
- Accepted, and deterministic:
  - "050.000" gives the same id as "50";
  - a power of MaxInt64 is accepted; the set caps it at MaxValidatorPower;
  - top-level and account keys are matched case-insensitively, but parameter keys are checked exactly;
  - duplicate top-level keys are merged the same way in both decoding passes.
- I found no safety problem.
- The node must not be required to hold its genesis key: after a key change it legitimately holds another.

Smoke run: I ran keygen, wrote a genesis file and started the server. /hdls/status served "smoke/ee229d...", the log printed the id, and a config with "networkId" was refused with: unknown field "networkId".

Mutants: 27 of my own, one at a time, in verify-S8-3 (script at <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S8-tools/mutants.py).
- 24 were caught. They cover every listed test:
  - the name, key, spelling, own-bank and seated-bank checks (rules 1, 2 and 5);
  - accounts not sorted, the bank not copied into state, height 1;
  - a zero balance refused, the cap compared with >= instead of >;
  - the delegate check, the parameter-presence check, strict decoding of the genesis;
  - the dynamic-mode snapshotPath rule, the signer bound to the bare name instead of the id, the node-name check;
  - an observer given the topology, lenient config decoding, the genesis left unvalidated;
  - the demo's bank and seat changes.
- 3 survived:
  - Acceptable(1), and the demo founder at power 2 (both reported above);
  - removing the sort of the topology names, which is pre-existing code with the same file order on every node, so not a problem.

Against the parent 3891341:
- The new cmd/server config_test.go fails 8 tests, among them TestLoadReadsTheGenesisFile and TestKeygenOutputLoads.
- The ledger and demo tests do not build there.
- Commits 178cd72 and 84c111d each build and vet, and pass the cmd and ledger tests.

Full suite, go1.27.3 with GOTOOLCHAIN=auto, all passed:
- gofmt -l printed nothing outside review/.
- go vet passed in the root and in ui.
- go build passed in the root and in ui.
- GOLEDGER_CHAOS_SLACK=4 go test -race -count=1 ./... passed twice: consensus about 55-59 s, node about 55 s, ledger about 10 s, cmd/server 1.4-1.6 s, cmd/demo 1 s.
- go test -C ui -race passed twice.
- go test -race -count=3 -run 'Chaos|Restart|SignLog|Resume|CatchUp' ./node/ passed in 91.9 s.

Naming follows the spelled-out rule. Dead code is removed (wellFormedKey, mustParseAmount, the old file types), and the comments are accurate apart from the commit 178cd72 claim noted above. The logs are in <scratch>/p2-scratch/verify-S8-logs/.
